  "acceptance": [
    {
      "id": "AC1",
      "text": "Ordered immutable root gates and cold-clone `make verify-E12-T10` pass. Evidence names the full source revision, lockfile/runtime versions, image digest and numeric limits: startup/readiness <=60 s, shutdown <=15 s, positive bounded body size and request deadline. Invalid/missing config/assets and preview or inherited harness credentials fail before public listen; successful startup accepts assigned PORT.",
      "textSha256": "7e174c4742c5a4739594e45303943624fffdb1553c37fbbf1fc9a51ec8c242f9",
      "predictionRefs": [
        "P1-config-build-bounds",
        "P2-wire-origin-cookies"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "AC2",
      "text": "The public origin always determines callback, redirect and invite origins. Host, Forwarded and X-Forwarded-* injection, external/encoded return paths and wrong origins cannot replace it. Cookies are separately emitted, Secure/HttpOnly and SameSite/path scoped; they contain no provider token, password, signing secret or PKCE verifier. Cookie mutations/logout require the configured Origin; bearer CLI requests have their explicit separate policy.",
      "textSha256": "485e8018a39b88364e6ab9db247681de893aad8c74d79486ad83c4ef0f06770f",
      "predictionRefs": [
        "P2-wire-origin-cookies",
        "P3-browser-auth-state"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "AC3",
      "text": "Dedicated fixture users complete real gateway-backed PKCE login and local deep-link return in browser evidence. Browser transaction binding, state, nonce, verifier, signature, audience, expiry and verified-email failures append no identity event. A stolen/other-browser transaction cannot log the victim into the attacker's account. Reused callbacks fail; established sessions survive restart with the stable private signing secret; an interrupted in-flight login safely restarts. Logout/revocation survives restart. Public cookies and logs never contain provider tokens or secrets.",
      "textSha256": "4a312703981a373360d9ca99ab1f20ab300b054dae90d9ef31930b66993eb1d3",
      "predictionRefs": [
        "P3-browser-auth-state",
        "P4-restart-authority"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "AC4",
      "text": "Two dedicated fixture identities create separate organizations. Private reads, writes and follow are refused across them and to an anonymous visitor. The hosted runtime exposes no raw stream/admin or fixture-login routes, starts without preview users/repos, and rejects agent execution/outbound integrations before their effect. The app surfaces Auth0/build state, disabled agents and reachable CLI-token settings; a newly signed-in user can create their own organization without seeded data.",
      "textSha256": "3c9ac124a97d21bf957002f00c36a4bed96254179a51bc79117caf95ec21f438",
      "predictionRefs": [
        "P5-private-capability-boundary",
        "P6-hosted-opaque-bearer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "AC5",
      "text": "The actual Railway service has a dedicated fresh private volume, one replica and zero overlapping mutation-serving revisions. `/healthz`, `/readyz`, asset loading, visible source identity and `/auth/login` work at its HTTPS origin. The manifest binds exact source/image/config/service/deployment. A controlled restart preserves a real operator's synthetic acceptance mutation and established login, documented by a minimal redacted UI/build/digest receipt; production identity is not dumped. The same immutable runtime's isolated dedicated-fixture restart proof independently replays byte-identical event prefixes/state. No public-fixture data or credentials were copied into this volume; no fixture-login seam is exposed to earn live proof.",
      "textSha256": "093678dbfe76a2db67c0e276d65ebab9a2a420026c0becf1a7a3f60194af45c0",
      "predictionRefs": [
        "P4-restart-authority",
        "P7-actual-railway-binding"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "AC6",
      "text": "Public provider evidence records actual issuer discovery/JWKS, web client ID and exact registered callback/logout/origin. The real operator can complete the deployed Auth0 login; capture a minimal redacted outcome bound to this revision, without a production token, password, private project, email or identity dump in evidence. Missing registration or a failed real callback remains an explicit blocker.",
      "textSha256": "a5088f4436e81703671cbde34fd3b78c03dcc0328c47683599d34de3e980a730",
      "predictionRefs": [
        "P8-actual-auth0-operator"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "AC7",
      "text": "Named journey `E12-T10 Auth0 login and private workspace` in configured project `proj-electric-forest-ms8w0nv1` covers changed browser paths with dedicated fixtures, zero console/page errors and DOM digests matching independently replayed dumps. Use the existing explicit `Replay: N/A (<reason>) + mitigation` fallback when unavailable. Real production credentials never enter an external QA recording.",
      "textSha256": "e5e92661ec8e84ff81abe2bf2ca0e8b25ab3fe3259d885910403453fc4a3e613",
      "predictionRefs": [
        "P9-browser-evidence-completeness"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "AC8",
      "text": "Two fresh committed readers agree before builder and after lifecycle writes; a fresh pre-critic freezes the finite threat model and a separate fresh critic alone verifies. Prior task ledgers, ceilings, controls and project stops are preserved.",
      "textSha256": "9c246934af440f3d2127e17a3b53bd63957047054045c4532237d66080d07831",
      "predictionRefs": [
        "P10-lifecycle-integrity"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "attacks": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "text": "Inject hostile origin/proxy/return values and cross-site POST/logout requests; verify exact refusal and unchanged stream heads. Restore HTTP or strip Secure in scratch: its corresponding sensor must go red.",
